WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
CMMC assessments provide a structured way to verify whether required cybersecurity

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.735
practices are implemented within a defined assessment scope.

00:00:07.735 --> 00:00:12.250
The required assessment type depends on the CMMC level and the applicable acquisition

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:12.890
requirement.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.955
A self-assessment is still a formal representation.

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:19.045
The organization needs knowledgeable personnel, accurate scope, reliable evidence,

00:00:19.045 --> 00:00:20.180
documented results,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.355
and accountable affirmation rather than an informal opinion about general security

00:00:24.355 --> 00:00:25.090
maturity.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.710
Some Level 2 contracts require an assessment by an authorized CMMC Third-Party Assessment

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.350
Organization.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.370
Level 3 uses the government assessment role established by the program.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.090
Organizations should confirm current assessor and status requirements through official

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:37.509
channels.

00:00:37.509 --> 00:00:39.520
Scope is a critical starting point.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.780
The assessment needs a clear understanding of systems, people, facilities, services,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.960
security-protection assets, external providers,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.040
and information flows associated with the covered contract information.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.710
Evidence may include policies, procedures, configurations, logs, tickets,

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.760
training records, diagrams, inventories, approvals, technical outputs, interviews,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.840
and demonstrations.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.985
Strong evidence reflects normal operation rather than material created only for an

00:01:02.985 --> 00:01:04.095
assessment.

00:01:04.095 --> 00:01:07.035
Assessment results can identify findings that require action.

00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:11.205
Program rules govern status, remediation, any permitted plan of action, affirmation,

00:01:11.205 --> 00:01:15.160
and reporting, so organizations should not assume that every gap can be deferred.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:19.400
Verification is a point-in-time activity supported by ongoing responsibility.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.830
Systems change, employees move, suppliers change, configurations drift,

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.020
and new vulnerabilities emerge after an assessment has ended.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.628
Audit readiness is therefore an operational condition.

00:01:28.628 --> 00:01:32.410
Clear ownership, current documentation, repeatable controls, retained evidence,

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.175
internal review,

00:01:33.175 --> 00:01:37.625
and timely remediation make assessment results more accurate and security outcomes more

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:38.100
sustainable.
